WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.384
In its early days, the capital of Shang moved quite often.

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:08.678
The old capital suffered floods, and the people's lives were unsettled.

00:00:09.028 --> 00:00:13.372
King Pan Geng decided to move the capital to Yin.

00:00:13.722 --> 00:00:18.018
He believed the new place was better suited to the country's growth.

00:00:18.368 --> 00:00:22.832
But some people did not want to move, and felt very uneasy.

00:00:23.182 --> 00:00:26.998
Again and again, Pan Geng patiently persuaded everyone.

00:00:27.348 --> 00:00:33.660
In the end, the people packed their belongings and set out with Pan Geng.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:38.258
The long procession slowly advanced toward the new capital.

00:00:38.608 --> 00:00:42.376
Yin became an important political center of the Shang dynasty.

00:00:42.726 --> 00:00:46.446
From then on, the Shang capital finally settled down.

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:52.844
Archaeologists discovered the Yin ruins at Anyang, finding oracle-bone script and bronze vessels.

00:00:53.194 --> 00:00:57.226
These discoveries help us understand life in the late Shang.

